{
  "dom_id": "step-q3243",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Find the $y$-intercept of the line that passes through the point $(-6,8)$ and has a slope of $\\frac{3}{2}.$",
  "worked_solution": "Since the line passes through the point $(-6,8)$ and its slope is $\\frac{3}{2}$, we substitute $x=-6$, $y=8,$ and $m=\\frac{3}{2}$ into the equation in slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =mx+b \\\\ (8) & =(\\frac{3}{2})(-6)+b \\\\ 8 & =-\\frac{18}{2}+b \\\\ 8 & =-9+b \\\\ 17 & =b \\\\ b & =17\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the $y$-intercept is $b=17.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
